course: dictionary
lesson: 6001
title: Meatless
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Meatless is built from two parts: meat, and -less, which means without. So meatless means without meat. Words like hopeless and careless are built the same way.
explain: «The whole family waits at the window for the first star, and only then the supper of dvanAdtsyat strav, twelve meatless dishes, begins.» The word meatless tells you what kind of dishes they are: dishes with no meat in them. Ask what word would fit: twelve without-meat dishes makes sense, so meatless fits.
explain: Context also shows where the word is used. Schools and families talk about meatless meals for healthy eating, such as a Meatless Monday. Some Christians eat meatless meals on Fridays or in Lent. Each time, the clue is the same: no meat.
fact: Meatless means without meat.
fact: The word has two parts: meat and -less, which means without.
fact: «Dvanadtsyat strav» is the Christmas Eve supper in Ukraine, with twelve meatless dishes.
fact: Meatless Monday is a day when people eat meatless meals, and some Christians eat meatless meals on Fridays or in Lent.
fact: A meatless meal can still have fish or mushrooms, as in the dishes of the Christmas Eve supper.
exercise: «The meal was meatless, with no meat on the plate.» What does meatless mean? | *Without meat | Very hungry | Made of wheat | With extra meat
exercise: «The whole family waits at the window for the first star, and only then the supper of dvanAdtsyat strav, twelve meatless dishes, begins.» Find and copy the one word that means without meat. | twelve | window | *meatless | supper
exercise: Nadia's school has a Meatless Monday. What does this day mean? | *A day when the lunches have no meat | A day with only sweets | A day when everyone must eat meat | A day with no school
test: «Some Christians eat meatless meals on Fridays or in Lent.» What does meatless mean here? | *Without meat | Very fast | Full of meat | Happy
test: Which part of meatless means without? | Ness | Mea | Meat | *-less
exam: «The twelve dishes of the supper are meatless, so none of them has meat.» What does meatless tell you? | *Without meat, so none has meat | Spicy | Frozen | Full of meat
